WEBVTT

00:00.470 --> 00:04.810
Oh please come down like an angel
Oh please come down like an angel

00:04.810 --> 00:12.540
Asano hitogomi o nagamete coffee nondeiru
Watching a crowd in the morning, and drinking coffee

00:13.450 --> 00:21.450
Aseri nado naikano youni hitoni wa mieru daro
People must see me as if I don't have any worries

00:22.090 --> 00:29.920
lma menomae ni atomodori dekinai jikan ga
I know that the time I will never be able to get back

00:30.710 --> 00:38.220
Tashika ni nagareteru koto o watashi wa shitteru
Is moving in front of me

00:38.440 --> 00:47.440
Marude kyou shika nai toiu ikikata o shitemita toki
If I live like today is the last day of my life

00:47.730 --> 00:55.490
Saisho ni nani ga mieru darou
I wonder what I can see first

00:56.570 --> 01:00.830
Oh please come down like an angel
Oh please come down like an angel

01:01.260 --> 01:09.260
Sore ga donnani chiisana hikari demo ii
I don't care no matter how small the light is

01:09.770 --> 01:11.770
Sugata o misete hoshii
I just wish to see its shape

01:11.770 --> 01:16.010
Oh please come down like an angel
Oh please come down like an angel

01:16.680 --> 01:22.470
lma no kimochi sonomama hanaseru
I want to meet someone

01:22.470 --> 01:22.680
Rumiko Takahashi Anthology
Mermaid Forest
lma no kimochi sonomama hanaseru
I want to meet someone

01:22.680 --> 01:29.190
Rumiko Takahashi Anthology
Mermaid Forest
Sonna hito ni deaitai
Who I can tell my honest feelings to

01:29.190 --> 01:30.980
Mermaid Forest
Rumiko Takahashi Anthology

01:50.580 --> 01:52.340
It's morning, Yuta.

01:52.550 --> 01:54.280
Oh, yeah.

01:57.920 --> 01:59.610
Where shall we go today?

02:00.820 --> 02:02.350
North or south.

02:02.760 --> 02:04.780
East or west.

02:05.430 --> 02:07.090
Let's have this make the decision.

02:12.830 --> 02:14.200
That way.

02:24.580 --> 02:25.980
Ouch.

02:26.110 --> 02:26.810
Hey.

02:28.080 --> 02:29.550
What's the matter, boy?

02:29.620 --> 02:31.050
You're hurt, aren't you?

02:31.820 --> 02:34.410
It's OK.
I've got my medicine.

02:50.140 --> 02:52.270
Hey, what did you just take?!

02:53.410 --> 02:57.940
Like I said, it's a medicine from home.
My mom told me to take it if I got hurt.

03:07.910 --> 03:12.460
Episode 8
The Last Face
(Part I)

03:22.400 --> 03:23.460
Nanao!

03:24.010 --> 03:26.970
Nanao, where are you?

03:28.340 --> 03:32.210
Strange. Where did he go
so early in the morning?

03:33.110 --> 03:34.480
Nanao!

03:36.080 --> 03:39.950
Run, Nanao. Run.

03:43.590 --> 03:45.150
You were kidnapped?

03:45.260 --> 03:50.060
Yeah. I was sleeping and
my grandma woke me up.

04:02.240 --> 04:03.940
<i>Take this as well.</i>

04:05.350 --> 04:07.910
She put me in a car that
a strange man was driving.

04:10.820 --> 04:13.790
<i>Are you hungry?</i>

04:16.890 --> 04:20.160
<i>I have to get back to Mom.</i>

04:21.430 --> 04:23.830
<i>It's hot.</i>
<i>Can I roll down the window?</i>

04:24.400 --> 04:26.160
<i>Yeah, I'll do it for you.</i>

04:31.510 --> 04:33.630
<i>Don't be stupid, stop!</i>

04:34.210 --> 04:35.200
<i>Let go of me!</i>

05:01.570 --> 05:03.830
I ran away from him.

05:04.410 --> 05:09.180
I see. But why did your grandma
make you take the urn?

05:09.180 --> 05:10.300
I don't know.

05:10.410 --> 05:11.670
What's in it?

05:12.650 --> 05:13.670
Bones, I think.

05:14.050 --> 05:16.280
Well, it usually is, but...

05:22.360 --> 05:26.660
Look. Can you not tell
my mom about this?

05:27.900 --> 05:29.560
That's fine, but why?

05:30.500 --> 05:35.230
The three of us live together,
me, my mom, and grandma.

05:36.340 --> 05:39.400
If my mom found out about this,
she'll be worried.

05:41.440 --> 05:45.610
Right. You can't tell her
your grandma had a part in it.

05:45.810 --> 05:47.940
OK. We won't say anything.

05:48.020 --> 05:49.680
Really? Thanks.

05:50.190 --> 05:52.090
But what are you going to
do with that urn?

05:53.050 --> 05:55.990
This?
Well, I'll figure something out.

05:55.990 --> 05:58.490
OK.
A secret, huh?

05:58.490 --> 05:59.550
Yeah.

06:07.570 --> 06:08.500
Nanao!

06:08.740 --> 06:10.810
Oh, Mom!

06:10.810 --> 06:15.000
Nanao! You're all right.
I was so worried.

06:15.640 --> 06:16.540
Mom.

06:16.540 --> 06:17.640
Nanao.

06:18.080 --> 06:20.100
You're hurt, aren't you?

06:20.280 --> 06:21.680
Oh, this.

06:21.750 --> 06:23.420
Did you take your medicine
like I told you to?

06:23.420 --> 06:25.110
Yeah, I did.

06:25.150 --> 06:26.550
Good.

06:27.590 --> 06:28.620
Hi.

06:28.620 --> 06:29.950
Hello.

06:35.860 --> 06:37.990
About our family's medicine?

06:38.070 --> 06:40.970
Yeah, you're making
him take it, right?

06:41.570 --> 06:44.200
It's not ordinary medicine, is it?

06:47.940 --> 06:50.140
Oh, it is miraculous, isn't it?

06:50.250 --> 06:52.150
It's a medicine handed down...

06:52.580 --> 06:55.670
in our family from ancient times,
it can heal small wounds instantly.

06:56.650 --> 06:58.980
Mom, I'm hungry.

06:59.150 --> 07:02.680
Oh, I'm sorry. I'll get
something ready right away.

07:03.290 --> 07:04.660
I'll come, too.

07:08.630 --> 07:11.700
"It is miraculous, isn't it?"
She says.

07:11.700 --> 07:13.830
Mana, what do you think?

07:14.270 --> 07:16.070
Isn't it from a mermaid?

07:21.680 --> 07:25.940
Nanao mustn't stay in this house.
Why did you bring him back?

07:27.020 --> 07:28.310
We shouldn't have?

07:32.450 --> 07:34.920
Nanao and his mother.

07:39.390 --> 07:40.990
A different woman.

07:42.730 --> 07:45.490
This boy looks like Nanao,
but it's not him, either.

07:46.370 --> 07:48.060
What does this mean?

07:49.070 --> 07:51.130
That Nanao and his mother are...

07:51.210 --> 07:52.540
Mother.

07:53.270 --> 07:56.210
What are you doing?
You don't know them.

08:00.950 --> 08:04.040
Oh, I'm sorry.
Did she say something to you?

08:04.350 --> 08:06.290
Not really.

08:06.690 --> 08:08.160
It looks great.

08:10.090 --> 08:13.960
It's delicious.
Come on, Yuta, try some.

08:14.760 --> 08:15.290
OK.

08:15.630 --> 08:17.290
Here you go.

08:19.130 --> 08:20.690
Thank you for the snack.

08:21.840 --> 08:22.930
See you!

08:23.370 --> 08:26.000
Bye, Yuta, Mana!

08:26.710 --> 08:27.830
See ya.

08:32.950 --> 08:36.380
Yuta, do you think he's one of us?

08:37.090 --> 08:40.420
I don't know. But we shouldn't
just leave him like this.

08:51.420 --> 08:52.230
RESTAURANT HAMAYA

08:52.230 --> 08:54.970
RESTAURANT HAMAYA
Oh, rumors about that house
with a storehouse?

08:54.970 --> 08:56.430
Oh, rumors about that house
with a storehouse?

08:56.570 --> 08:58.100
Yes, yes, yes.

08:58.140 --> 09:02.410
The wife divorced her husband
who was president of some company.

09:02.480 --> 09:04.970
Oh, no, we didn't mean
those kind of stories.

09:05.250 --> 09:08.150
When they broke up,
they fought over their only son...

09:08.150 --> 09:10.170
and it led to some sort of bloodshed.

09:10.550 --> 09:11.490
Oh.

09:11.490 --> 09:13.960
The wife doted over
her son so much and...

09:13.960 --> 09:16.260
rather than losing him
to her husband...

09:16.260 --> 09:20.320
she dragged the dying boy into
the storehouse and fed him poison.

09:20.660 --> 09:21.320
<i>Poison?</i>

09:23.160 --> 09:26.170
In the end, the widowed mother of
the husband took the young boy...

09:26.170 --> 09:28.500
and he survived, I heard.

09:28.640 --> 09:32.900
Rumor has it that the wife was left
with a terrible scar on her face.

09:34.040 --> 09:36.440
But when we went there today,
the boy was there and...

09:36.440 --> 09:38.140
his mother didn't have
any scar on her face.

09:38.410 --> 09:41.080
Oh, different people live there now.

09:41.080 --> 09:44.420
What I just told you
happened 25 years ago.

09:44.850 --> 09:45.910
25 years ago.

09:46.220 --> 09:52.650
I forgot his name, but that young boy
was my grade school classmate.

09:52.790 --> 09:55.000
I don't know what's
become of him after that.

09:55.000 --> 09:57.400
He was taken in by the
relatives on his father's side.

09:57.830 --> 09:59.820
<i>Different people.</i>

10:18.350 --> 10:21.250
<i>Nanao! Stay with me!</i>
<i>It's your grandma!</i>

10:21.520 --> 10:23.820
<i>Your mother poisoned you,</i>
<i>didn't she, Nanao?!</i>

10:25.330 --> 10:29.090
<i>Mom, help me. Mom.</i>

10:29.900 --> 10:32.530
<i>Please, please take</i>
<i>good care of Nanao.</i>

10:32.530 --> 10:33.230
<i>Yes.</i>

10:36.070 --> 10:36.930
<i>Go.</i>

10:40.140 --> 10:49.210
Nanao, Nanao,
I promise I'll come and get you.

11:21.680 --> 11:26.140
You said Nanao was
showing the urn to them.

11:27.720 --> 11:29.250
You tried to make him
run away, didn't you?

11:31.830 --> 11:35.350
Don't interfere with me.
Do you hear?

11:57.650 --> 11:58.910
Nanao.

12:14.040 --> 12:15.500
See you tomorrow.

12:15.500 --> 12:16.770
Bye-bye!

12:18.340 --> 12:20.900
Oh, Yuta, Mana.

12:21.780 --> 12:23.540
Hey, Nanao.

12:23.640 --> 12:25.510
I didn't know you worked here.

12:26.250 --> 12:28.340
You have to work
if you want to eat, you know?

12:28.720 --> 12:29.510
Right.

12:29.620 --> 12:33.350
By the way, how long has your mom
been making you take that medicine?

12:33.620 --> 12:37.320
Well, I started in
grade school, I think.

12:37.660 --> 12:40.560
I used to vomit a little blood
sometimes when I was little.

12:41.500 --> 12:42.390
Hey!

12:42.760 --> 12:44.760
And she still made you take it?

12:45.000 --> 12:47.260
Yeah, she said I just
had to put up with it.

12:47.640 --> 12:49.830
<i>What's she thinking?</i>

12:50.470 --> 12:54.270
Promise me! Don't ever take it again!
Even if your mom gives it to you!

12:55.940 --> 12:56.880
Promise him.

12:56.980 --> 12:57.540
I promise.

12:57.780 --> 12:58.510
Good.

12:58.850 --> 13:00.870
But why?

13:02.180 --> 13:02.770
It's him.

13:05.990 --> 13:07.420
That's the man who kidnapped me.

13:12.190 --> 13:13.160
Yuta?

13:14.330 --> 13:15.660
I'll go talk to him.

13:19.530 --> 13:23.970
I heard you tried to take him away
without his mother knowing.

13:26.310 --> 13:27.100
Why?

13:28.940 --> 13:30.930
His mother is...

13:34.150 --> 13:35.080
Hey.

13:37.750 --> 13:40.190
Mana, take Nanao home.
I'll follow him.

13:40.290 --> 13:41.480
Mana, take Nanao home.
I'll follow him.

13:41.720 --> 13:43.990
OK.
Be careful, Yuta.

13:44.260 --> 13:44.850
Yeah.

13:49.010 --> 13:58.940
Rumiko Takahashi Anthology
Mermaid Forest

14:08.850 --> 14:09.940
It's me.

14:16.020 --> 14:17.550
I understand.

14:34.740 --> 14:35.770
Mother.

14:36.810 --> 14:39.110
You're using the
mermaid flesh again.

14:40.410 --> 14:43.950
Haven't I told you many times that no one
in our family has become immortal...

14:43.950 --> 14:47.650
by eating the handed down
mermaid flesh?

14:48.090 --> 14:51.080
It's a poison.
Yet you...

14:53.830 --> 14:56.020
Nanao is my child.

14:56.530 --> 15:00.560
I won't let anyone take him.
No matter what you say.

15:04.370 --> 15:05.700
<i>Nanao...</i>

15:07.070 --> 15:09.410
Hey, is Yuta going to be OK?

15:09.980 --> 15:12.670
No worries.
He knows what he's doing.

15:23.620 --> 15:24.650
Mom.

15:44.180 --> 15:47.810
She's not coming out.
What's she doing?

15:47.880 --> 15:51.980
I don't know. I'm not allowed
to go inside the storehouse.

16:03.900 --> 16:04.890
Who's that?

16:05.130 --> 16:05.930
I don't know.

16:13.010 --> 16:14.940
<i>She resembles that woman.</i>

16:15.410 --> 16:17.840
<i>Nanao and his mother.</i>

16:18.680 --> 16:21.340
<i>She resembles the</i>
<i>woman in the photograph.</i>

16:40.370 --> 16:42.300
<i>Is he waiting for someone?</i>

17:02.320 --> 17:03.480
<i>That woman.</i>

17:05.690 --> 17:08.790
Nanao.
You're Nanao, aren't you?

17:09.660 --> 17:10.250
<i>Nanao?</i>

17:10.660 --> 17:13.220
Mother.

17:18.240 --> 17:21.540
Are you really my mother?

17:21.540 --> 17:23.200
Yes, Nanao.

17:23.880 --> 17:27.340
<i>They're a mother and son?</i>
<i>It's got to be a joke.</i>

17:27.780 --> 17:31.240
<i>She's too young and</i>
<i>why is she calling him Nanao?</i>

17:31.820 --> 17:36.450
See, this mirror.
I've treasured it all this time.

17:37.430 --> 17:42.490
You bought it for me,
by saving up your small allowance.

17:43.030 --> 17:44.460
You made me so happy.

17:45.130 --> 17:46.500
Mother.

17:48.300 --> 17:50.700
Give me back my son, Nanao!

18:00.010 --> 18:01.070
What have you done?!

18:02.480 --> 18:04.420
Hey! Who on earth are you!

18:06.950 --> 18:07.920
<i>That scar.</i>

18:28.340 --> 18:31.210
Hey, man, wake up.

18:32.780 --> 18:39.980
Nanao...The Nanao
that woman is raising is my son.

18:40.960 --> 18:44.550
Hey, she called you Nanao.
What does that mean?

18:45.330 --> 18:50.390
She's my mother. From whom
I was taken away 25 years ago, my...

18:50.800 --> 18:52.100
<i>25 years ago.</i>

18:54.900 --> 18:55.990
<i>That photograph.</i>

18:59.040 --> 19:01.840
Hey!
She ate mermaid flesh, didn't she?

19:02.480 --> 19:04.140
How did you know?

19:04.250 --> 19:06.350
I also ate it.

19:06.350 --> 19:09.050
That's why I can tell
that woman's face.

19:09.050 --> 19:10.380
It's from the poison of a mermaid.

19:11.690 --> 19:16.450
Twenty five years ago,
she and I ate mermaid flesh.

19:17.590 --> 19:20.560
She forced me to.

19:20.930 --> 19:23.730
I couldn't help spitting it out
because of the burning pain...

19:24.270 --> 19:27.360
but I was still left
with a permanent scar.

19:27.640 --> 19:28.800
You too?

19:29.470 --> 19:32.840
I'm still getting older
as you can see.

19:33.110 --> 19:35.410
But my mother, who I saw today,
hasn't changed...

19:35.410 --> 19:38.940
since the day I was
taken away 25 years ago.

19:39.350 --> 19:41.640
She's as young as
she was back then.

19:42.380 --> 19:44.580
And eight years ago...

19:45.250 --> 19:47.190
she appeared in front
of me out of the blue...

19:47.190 --> 19:50.160
and took my son away,
who had just turned two.

19:50.890 --> 19:53.230
They disappeared.

19:53.230 --> 19:57.320
I kept looking for them,
and I finally found them.

19:57.460 --> 20:00.490
My grandmother contacted me
that my mother came back...

20:01.040 --> 20:04.030
with a child that she calls Nanao.
The same as my name.

20:07.610 --> 20:09.130
So he can take your place?

20:09.240 --> 20:10.640
I don't know.

20:10.780 --> 20:14.840
I don't know what
she's going to do with him.

20:16.080 --> 20:19.950
<i>If the woman we just saw</i>
<i>had taken Nanao away...</i>

20:20.290 --> 20:23.650
<i>who's the woman living in the</i>
<i>house that Nanao calls "Mom"?</i>

20:26.630 --> 20:28.990
Hey!
Wake up! Hey!

20:31.530 --> 20:32.400
Mom.

20:33.130 --> 20:36.100
This is weird.
I saw her come in here.

20:36.870 --> 20:39.740
Mom, where are you?

20:42.340 --> 20:45.550
<i>These are the clothes she was</i>
<i>wearing when she came in here.</i>

20:45.550 --> 20:46.510
<i>What's this?</i>

20:49.820 --> 20:53.480
<i>Bloody bandages?</i>
<i>What are these?</i>

20:54.590 --> 20:56.020
What's this box?

21:14.170 --> 21:15.400
<i>A face...</i>

21:16.240 --> 21:19.770
<i>It's a human face</i>
<i>that's been skinned off.</i>

21:31.630 --> 21:36.620
<i>The woman who ate mermaid flesh and</i>
<i>abducted Nanao when he was a baby.</i>

21:37.200 --> 21:41.690
<i>The woman who's raising Nanao, giving</i>
<i>him the medicine that heals wounds.</i>

21:44.270 --> 21:46.400
Nanao, run away.

21:47.110 --> 21:51.100
She's a dreadful woman.

21:51.810 --> 21:53.010
Nanao.

21:53.780 --> 21:55.770
What are you doing, Mana?

21:58.990 --> 22:00.680
Mana!

22:24.990 --> 22:33.490
Mukashi no koto datowa mada katazuke rarenai
It's just something in the past, but I still can't forget it

22:34.870 --> 22:43.380
ltsumade kakaruno to anata wa warau kedo
"How long does it take?" You smiled at me

22:44.840 --> 22:53.720
Dorekurai oboete iru hidoku naki nagara
How much do you remember? I cried hard

22:54.770 --> 23:04.270
Dorekurai oboete iru anokoto to ieba
How much do you remember if I talk about "that thing"?

23:09.360 --> 23:18.370
ltsumademo mada utsumuite
I still look down

23:19.330 --> 23:27.840
Tobikoe rarenai mizutamari
I can't jump over the puddle

23:28.970 --> 23:38.480
Wakaranakunaru moshikasuruto
I'm confused

23:38.810 --> 23:48.320
Kawarenai no wa watashi dake kana
Maybe I'm the only one who still can't change

23:53.280 --> 24:02.830
Mukashi no koto datowa mada katazuke rarenai
It's just something in the past, but I still can't forget it

24:06.310 --> 24:09.010
Stop it! What are you doing to Mana?

24:09.780 --> 24:11.810
You're Nanao's mother, aren't you?

24:13.750 --> 24:15.960
The wounds on
her cheeks have healed.

24:15.960 --> 24:18.290
You've eaten mermaid flesh,
haven't you?

24:19.460 --> 24:23.290
What happened in this
storehouse 25 years ago?

24:24.570 --> 24:28.970
You're not going to?
No! It's poisonous! Don't eat it!

24:29.970 --> 24:30.990
Episode 9 "The Last Face, Part II".

24:30.990 --> 24:33.870
Episode 9
The Last Face
(Part II)
Episode 9 "The Last Face, Part II".

